<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Okinawa Reversion Agreement</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1971">1971</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Okinawa Reversion Agreement was a treaty between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, signed on 17 June 1971, under which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ryukyu-islands">Ryukyu Islands</a>, administered by the United States since 1945, returned to Japanese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> on 15 May 1972. The United States kept its military bases on Okinawa under the Japan–US security treaty, and the agreement became controversial for secret arrangements on nuclear weapons and costs.</p></div>
